From 3a606bf58745fbc7de1af4d4f7f3a8198699b563 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jinwli <islijw@163.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:58:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: Add support for HCI Enhanced Accept Synchronous
 Connection Request

Add support for HCI_OP_ENHANCED_ACCEPT_SYNC_CONN_REQ (0x043e) to accept
incoming SCO/eSCO connections with the full coding format parameters
instead of only the legacy HCI_OP_ACCEPT_SYNC_CONN_REQ (0x0429) which can
only express the air mode via the voice setting.

The enhanced accept is used only when both the controller reports support
for the command in its command support table and the driver has explicitly
enabled it via the new HCI_QUIRK_ENHANCED_ACCEPT_SYNC_CONN quirk. Unlike
the enhanced setup command the enhanced accept command has its own
supported commands bit (commands[29] bit 0x10).

Both the non-deferred accept path in hci_conn_request_evt and the deferred
accept path in sco_conn_defer_accept now send the enhanced accept command
when capable, filling in the coding format parameters based on the air
mode from the voice setting (CVSD or transparent data).

hci_qca enables the quirk for controllers with the new
QCA_CAP_ENHANCED_ACCEPT_SYNC_CONN capability following the same pattern as
the HFP hardware offload support.

Signed-off-by: jinwli <islijw@163.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c      | 17 +++++++++--
 include/net/bluetooth/hci.h      | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h | 10 +++++++
 net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c         | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 net/bluetooth/hci_event.c        | 34 +++++++++++++++-------
 net/bluetooth/sco.c              | 23 +++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 159 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
